/-!
# Locally uniform holomorphic relative Fourier inverses

For the original varying period family, the actual Fourier symbol in its
proved marked frame depends holomorphically on the base at each fixed
frequency. Select a maximal coordinate at a fixed centre. There is one
common open neighborhood on which every nonzero frequency retains a
positive elliptic lower bound in that same selected coordinate. The
reciprocal multipliers are holomorphic there and have uniform inverse-
frequency estimates for the original integer modes.

No convergence of parameter-dependent Fourier sums or higher-direct-image
comparison is asserted by this package.
-/
